From: <worker git identity, redacted>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:58:39 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Tell a repaired checkout from the recorded worktree

The owner token lives in the worktree's admin directory. When the
checkout is deleted, rebuilt at the same path and reattached with
`git worktree repair`, git keeps that directory and its token, and only
writes a new `.git` file. With inode numbers reused, cleanup and the
failure report still offered `git worktree remove` for the new checkout.

Identity now also records the `.git` file's change time, which a new
file always gets fresh and which userspace cannot set back. A malformed
owner token now just fails to match instead of raising
UnicodeDecodeError out of cleanup and the report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
